The original is a Hermes Agent plugin in Python: fifteen tools over the Yandex
Disk REST API v1, a path module that confines every path to an optional root
folder, an action allow-list applied at registration, and a load-time probe of
whether the token may use Yandex's search endpoint. This rewrite keeps the
tools, the endpoints and their query parameters, the OAuth header, the two
request shapes (the Deferred operation polled to completion, and the two-step
transfer that never shows the token to the transfer host), the path
normalisation and the sandbox, the action groups, the refusal sentences and
the guards on a download (a complete file or an older one left alone), all in
Common Lisp over the image's own HTTP call. What changed: an answer is
rendered as lines a model reads instead of a JSON envelope, the search
capability probe is not run at load (the tool answers Yandex's refusal
instead, so a token that may not search still has every other tool), and the
action allow-list withholds a tool at start rather than at import. What was
left out: the environment-variable plumbing of Hermes itself (the values live
in the cell's config section), the Hermes load-time budget the probe was
sized for, and the emoji each Hermes tool carried.
